keiichi: Hey, Rena...[pdl] Is there something...[pxl] that everyone is keeping from me?
rena: Huh?[pxl] No.[pm] Not at all.
keiichi: ...[pdl] You're lying,[pl] aren't you?
Rena suddenly stopped.
Her expression was cold and intense.
rena: What do you mean by that,[p] Keiichi-kun?
Her tone was still the same cheery and lighthearted one as before.
keiichi: You are,[pm] aren't you? [p]...[pl]Keeping something from me?
After understanding what I meant,[pm] her expression grew even more intense.
Seeing that face,[p] I regretted saying something so rash.
...[pm]But she came back at me in a way I didn't expect.
rena: Well then,[pm] Keiichi-kun.[pxl] Aren't you keeping something from us?
Her tone didn't change,[p] but it was the first time I'd seen this expression from her.
With how her gaze pierced through me,[pm] I couldn't believe this was the same Rena.
rena: Aren't you?[pxl] Lies[pl] or secrets.[pxl] ...Aren't you?
You are.[pxl] Secrets.
She didn't actually say that part,[pm] but she looked as if she did.
The incident with Tomitake-san,[p] and how I felt alienated from the group.
Even without having to think about it,[pl] there were things I knew I felt guilty about.
But[p]...[pxl] I didn't tell everyone about what happened with Tomitake-san[pxl]... to be considerate.
I was keeping it a secret just the same way they didn't tell me about Oyashiro-sama.
Then[p]...[pxl] aren't we even[p]...?
keiichi: No,[pm] I'm not.[pxl] No lies.[pl] Nor secrets.
rena: Liar.
Her answer was instant[pm] and it shook me.
Rena stared as if burrowing through me.
Watching me.[pm] Like a hawk.
keiichi: Why would you say that I'm lying?
rena: Didn't you say that you were called into the teacher's room yesterday during the club meeting, Keiichi-kun?
rena: I know[p]...[pxl] you didn't go to the teacher's room.
I swallowed hard.
It clearly wasn't a bluff.[pl] She knew what happened.
rena: The teacher said you had a guest,[p] didn't she?
rena: But you didn't talk at the entrance.[pl] You talked inside of a car near the school gate.[pl] With some man we don't know.
Rena knew everything.
She knew that I was called out by Ooishi-san[p] and that I heard about the incident with Tomitake-san as well.[pl] Did she know all of it?!
rena: Exactly who was that man?
keiichi: [lspeed=0.05]I-I [lspeed=0.02]don't know him!
rena: Why did someone you don't know have business with you?
keiichi: I[p]...[pm] I want to know that myself!
rena: Then what did you talk about?
keiichi: It has nothing to do with you guys...!
It was a lie.
[wait time="2.0" hide_text="false"]
rena: LIES!!!
Rena's scream echoed through the trees...
Sending frightened birds into the air.
I couldn't exhale the deep breath I had just taken.
No.[p] It was like I wasn't allowed to exhale.
It was here...[p] I first realized.
The person standing in front of me...[pxl] She wasn't Rena Ryuugu.
Then,[p] who was it that was standing before me now?
Who had assumed Rena Ryuugu's appearance?
I held my breath for so long I could feel myself suffocating...
rena: Right?
And then she made a facial expression that Rena normally might have made.
It didn't matter that it was Rena's usual smile...[pl] It chilled me to the bone.
She drew closer to me.
I felt her breath against my face.
It wasn't the least bit exciting.
Whoever this was with Rena's face was going to chew my nose right off!
...I cowered as I imagined that.
Then,[p] she smirked as if she could see right through me.
rena: We also have secrets~[pl] ...just like how Keiichi-kun has secrets~.
It was Rena's usual smile...[pl] but her eyes were still like that of a hawk's.
Bringing her face close enough to mine to almost bump into my nose...[pm] she "kindly" persuaded me.
I couldn't nod or shake my head.
This person standing in front of me...[pxl] this person who looked like Rena,[pl] frightened me to my core.
I was terrified knowing that she could hear the sound of me swallowing nervously.
[wait time="2.0"]
After what felt like an eternity,[p] she finally spoke.
rena: Let's go.[p] It's getting chilly.
It was Rena again.
Smiling at me once more,[p] she started walking as if nothing at all had happened.
...[pl]When I was released from her gaze,[p] my legs gave out from under me[p] and I slumped onto the ground.
...[pl]I wasn't able to lift a finger until Rena was out of sight.
keiichi: Who was...[pm] that...?
I felt cold.[pxl] My body was drenched in sweat.
I was finally able to form a coherent thought[pl] and asked myself once again.
Who was...[pl] that person...[pxl] who looked like Rena Ryuugu?
